Hello, everyone! From April 29 to May 20, Royal Quest is hosting a massive — "Warlord’s Day" event! In this guide, we'll show you how to follow in General Maximus’ footsteps, defeat the army of undead and earn as many rewards as possible!

How to join the event? 

Look for the quest "Mysterious Scroll: New Information" in your task list and talk to Omnis the Lab Assistant next to the fountain in Varlone. In the next quest, "Details?” Omnis will tell you that he needs a part from an ancient device and send you to Employee Luther. 

How do I start hunting N'Galu's minions? 

Coworker Luther will offer you a deal: a crucial part from an ancient device in exchange for wiping out the evil creatures threatening the world of Aura. Starting the quest "Talk Later", you’ll need to head out to take down the minions of the dark forces leader:

• To Baron Logart’s Island for the Fire Irex; 
• To Arcon for Dark Morius;
• To Eltane for Cardigan’s Courier;
• To the Dead City for the Unholy Rebel;
• To Teuton for General Hrungnir.

As soon as you approach one of them, you'll automatically be given the guard’s uniform. This will grant you additional attack and defense abilities that will help in battle. Those skills will vary depending on your hero class.

What do I get for defeating the undead?  

1. After defeating these bosses, players receive a special trophy for their collection, which gives +1 to each character’s parameter permanently: Lord Ngalu’s General’s Helmet, Cardigan’s Courier’s Flamethrower, Unholy Rebel’s Paw, Fire Irex’s Head, Dark Morius’ Helmet; 
2. Daily quests to defeat these bosses allow you to obtain the Protector’s Reward set, which contains unique event items; 
3. By collecting 10 Pieces of Award from the Protector’s Reward set, you can create the Card of the Undead Victor. It will allow you to upgrade your weapon to get +3% to Attack, +5% to Critical Damage, +20% damage against Undead (two-handed), +12% damage against Undead (one-handed);
4. During the event, Ghosts of War sometimes appear in the spots where monsters have been killed. If a player kills a Ghosts of War while wearing guard’s uniform, Military Tokens drop. These can be used to craft a special amulet, the Honorary Commander's Badge. It will allow the hero to remain in guard’s uniform for unlimited time.
5. Throughout the event, Guard’s Emblem drop from all monsters.  They temporarily transform the hero into a guard. 

What achievements can I earn? 

• Royal Guard. You need to transform into a guard 10 times. For this, you’ll receive the "Kingdom Guard" title.

See you in Royal Quest!

Hello, everyone! As part of the April 17 update, here's what's changing in the game:

— Dear friends, we would like to treat you with another nice bonus! All players that have unlocked the Seasonal Adventure and already earned any number of Questles before the beginning of maintenance works, will get 500 more Questles as a gift!

Improvements/Fixes

-       Confettus logic has been changed. Instead of appearing at the Sky Fair, it will now spawn simultaneously in 4 locations: Iris, Illayr, Elgore and Quedock. Players will receive a corresponding notification. The reward system for defeating it has been updated too: players no longer receive a Toy Box for killing it, but can now choose their own reward upon completing the daily quest, "A Good Piñata Should be Big". Confettus’ health points have also been been reduced to 50 000 000;

-       The issue when players encountered the "Connection closed, code 21" error after using the "Tor Toise’s Sealing Wax" item, has been fixed;

-       The issue when the usage of "Sack of 'Celebrations' Powder" removed previously applied DoT (Damage over Time) effects, has been fixed;

-       The issue when players were able to kill Confettus with a single hit after using Card of the Shirra, has been fixed;

-       The issue with new monsters not spawning in the Sky Fair Arena has been fixed;

-       The description of «Elixirs of the Wise Dragon" in the guild shop has been fixed;

-       Navigation accuracy while completing the "Rat Affairs: I’ll Hunt You Down!" quest has been improved;

-       The issue with Neatnik 5.0 not granting the “+2 dodge” bonus has been fixed.

Hello! As part of the update on April 10, 2025, we’re here to tell you what’s changing in the game: 


In-Game Events

 — The Sky Fair event is live. As part of this activity, players will gain access to the "Unbridled Fun" Seasonal Adventure where they can earn over many rewards. You can read more about the event in our article here.

Economy

— To celebrate Royal Quest's birthday, applying item tranzamples is free for the whole Sky Fair duration;
— Players logging in at least once using any gaming platform during the Sky Fair will receive 50 Norin’s Hyperbags. The gifts will be credited to the Golden Chest after logging in with any character on the player’s account;
— "The Pre-Holiday Prep Packs" promo has been launched.

New Features

— A new "Vehicle Panel" element has been added to the game. It consists of two slots: a vehicle icon and its resource;
— When interacting with the Ashkalot merchant, minimum and maximum prices for items currently listed on the market are now displayed. For weapons and gear, prices are only shown if there’s at least one such item on the market without upgrades, cards, or seals;
— "Neatnik 5.0", a new vehicle has been added to the game;
—A new set of "Bordeaux"-styled tranzamples has been introduced;
—A "Festive Delight" decoration has been added (adds +5% to maximum health).
— Class restrictions on using tranzamples have been removed. Players can now apply them to any piece of gear currently equipped, regardless of their class, as long as the item type matches;

Improvements

— To improve account security, additional rules for entering the four-digit password when logging into the game have been added;
— All loading screen images have been updated;
— The anti-bot system has been improved.

Huge thanks to the players and External Test Academy alumni helping us improve the game every day!

