Hello everyone! Introducing the March 25 update and what's going to change in the game:

Game Economy

—"Packs of Perfection" and "Sealing Wax Packs" promos have been added. 

What’s New

— Starting slot number for all new characters in the “Equipment”, “Consumables”, “Trophies” and “Craft” tabs has been increased from 17 to 36 cells. The change does not affect the number of slots on already created characters (their number of slots remains unchanged). If your current character has less than 36 slots in the corresponding inventory tab and you have created a new character with expanded slots, the missing slots will be discounted for previously created characters.
— Automatic detection of game language at the first launch in Steam has been added. The game language now depends on Steam interface language;
— First phase of party matchmaking mechanics has been added.

How it works?

1.	The matchmaking works within the party leader's location based on the difference in character levels;
2.	Initially, players with a difference of up to 5 levels are being searched for, with time this difference increases to a maximum of 25 levels;
3.	If the party leader moves to a new location, the matchmaking continues there.
4.	Parties are merged automatically;
5.	The leader of the biggest party will become the leader of the common one;
6.	Matchmaking disables when the party reaches 8 players or when the leader turns it off;
7.	The leader can turn on matchmaking if there are less than 8 players in the party;
8.	The search icon will be visible only to the party leader with new players joining immediately.

Stay tuned for more matchmaking mechanics updates and improvements!

Huge thanks to External Testing Academy for helping us making the game better every day!

Here’s what you need to do:

1.	Apply tags to Royal Quest in Steam Store. You can do it by clicking on “+” icon, located under the game description in “Popular user-defined tags for this product” section;

2.	Leave a comment listing the tags you applied. For example: “magic”, “MMORPG”, etc.;

3.	Authors of all such comments left between February 27, 1 PM (CET), and March 3, 1 PM (CET), will receive x100 Eltanite. The rewards will be credited to players’ accounts during upcoming maintenance works.

We appreciate your support and looking forward for your tags! Thank you for being there for us ❤️

New Party-Finding Mechanic

Looking for comrades is now becoming easier! New mechanic arrives in Royal Quest

A brand-new party-finding interface is coming to the game on February 11!

That’s how it works:

- the search occurs in the location you are in while taking into account the difference in character levels;
- the search starts with the level difference of 5, then it extends by 5 levels with each minute passed finally reaching the maximum level difference of 25;
- if you move to another location, the search continues there.
But that’s not all:

- parties are merged automatically;

- the leader of a larger party becomes the leader of a merged party;
- the search is off either when a party has 8 players, or when the leader turns the search off;
- a leader can initiate the search if their party has less than 8 players;
- the search icon is visible only to the party leader, while new players join the party immediately.

The party-finding mechanic will be improved and get new features in the future. What would you add to it? Share with us in the comments!

How does Royal Quest Online Marketplace work?

Greetings, brave hero! Did you know that in Royal Quest Online you can sell and buy in-game items through Steam Marketplace?

How to start trading?

- Make sure the item is not Account bound;.
- Stackabke items must be split into pieces;
- Talk to one of the Maidens to unlock  Steam Inventory;
- Transfer items to your inventory to put them up for sale, or pick up purchases from other players.

Which items are available for trading?

On Steam you can trade some popular items, including:

- Visuals: Da Gee, Cloud Deity;
- Resources: Philosopher's Stones, Arconite Sealing Wax, Rune of Preservation;
- Various Boxes and Sets: Souvenirs from the East, Dragon Treasures;
- And much more.

The list of items available for trade will be replenished regularly!

Have you already used Royal Quest Online Marketplace? Tell us about your Buy & Sale deals in the comments!

Dear friends,
